stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    %% ============================================================
    %% Proposer Sub-State FSM (6 states)
    %% ============================================================
    %% Proposer drives the Paxos protocol.
    %% This is the most complex of the 3 role sub-states.
    %% ============================================================

    [*] --> Idle

    Idle --> Preparing : propose(value)
    Preparing --> WaitingForPromises : PermissionRequest dispatched

    WaitingForPromises --> WaitingForPromises : accumulate\nPermissionGranted / Nack
    WaitingForPromises --> ProposerAccepting : grant quorum reached →\nSuggestion dispatched
    WaitingForPromises --> Aborted : nack quorum reached

    ProposerAccepting --> ProposerAccepting : accumulate\nAccepted / Nack
    ProposerAccepting --> Decided : accept quorum reached →\nDecided broadcasted

    Aborted --> Idle : retry policy\n(not in v0)

    %% --- Simulation Control (not protocol-level) ---
    %% ProposerInactive is entered/exited via simulator Control messages,
    %% not via Paxos protocol messages.
    %% This is the state that causes failwith in is_quorum_reached —
    %% it's structurally in the same sum type but semantically excluded
    %% from protocol operations.

    Idle --> ProposerInactive : MakeNodeInactive\n[Simulation Control]
    ProposerInactive --> Idle : ActivateNode\n— restore from Storage\n[Simulation Control]

    note right of ProposerInactive
        Simulation-level, not protocol-level.
        Node must recover from Storage to rejoin.
        ⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯
        This state is why is_quorum_reached
        still has a runtime failwith — the type
        system sees it as a sibling of active states.
    end note

    note right of Decided
        Terminal state for this round.
        Simple Paxos: one round, one decision.
    end note
